    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1204">

                <pb facs="1210" n="1200" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3393/3–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-14T10:00:00+08:00">March 14, 1949—10
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 14—12:46 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>118. Badger planning transfer some 600 men of 3rd Marines now based Tsingtao
                    aboard USS <hi rendition="#italic">Chilton</hi> to Shanghai relieve 9th Marines
                    after March 15. Also tentative plan for second trip south with flagship about
                    end March whereafter no longer base flagship Tsingtao but move about freely as
                    floating headquarters. Cruisers and destroyers also become more mobile, not
                    consider Tsingtao main station Service squadron, with reduced number vessels
                    remaining Tsingtao, also shore patrol of one company Marines retained in
                    barracks on Kuangsi Road. Expect <pb facs="1211" n="1201" xml:id="pg1201"/>
                    Badger devote more attention to southeast Asia view disorders there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
